adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET)
  return 403;
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset (i.e., `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is `undefined`) and the request does not include that header (so the header lookup also yields `undefined`), then `undefined !== undefined` is false and the request is treated as authenticated, creating an auth bypass under common misconfiguration. Additionally, there is no `req.method` guard, so the endpoint will process non-POST methods as long as other checks pass. The constant-time-compare point is more of a hardening suggestion, but the unset-secret bypass and missing method guard are verifiable in the diff.
